# Personal Info

This file is the agent's "who is the user" reference. Every research session reads it at start-up to calibrate how to interact, what conventions to follow, and how to talk to the user.

The format below is the v1 schema. Agents reading this file should be able to find each field by header. If you're updating fields manually, keep the headers exact.

## Identity

- **Name:** <NAME>
- **Current role:** <ROLE>

## History

### Academic
<ACADEMIC_HISTORY>

### Work
<WORK_HISTORY>

## How I work

### Tools and languages
<PROGRAMMING_LANGUAGES_AND_TOOLS>

### Research interests
<RESEARCH_AREAS>

### Interaction style
<INTERACTION_STYLE_NOTES>

## Operating preferences

- **Git fluency:** <novice | occasional | fluent>
- **Mode:** <claude.ai-only | also-local>
- **Home repo:** <HOME_REPO>
- **Codename base:** <FIRST_NAME_OR_SHORT_HANDLE>
- **Git commit email:** <EMAIL>

`Codename base` is the leading token of the per-session agent codename that RESEARCHER.md §2.0b constructs at session start. Format: `<Codename base> (web, <REPO>, <YYYYMMDDTHHMM>)`. The full codename is set as `user.name` for git commits *and* is the timestamp portion of the session's convo filename (so `git log` and `docs/active/<branch>/convos/` cross-reference by inspection). Default at bootstrap: your first name. Override to a shorter handle if you prefer (e.g., `DP`, `Prof-Smith`). `Git commit email` is set as `user.email` for the same commits — the address you want GitHub to attribute agent commits to.

`Home repo` is the catch-all GitHub repo for personal / non-research-project tasks. Used by the `task-create` skill (override target when the user says "my personal list" or similar) and `task-remind` (second query target at session-start). Default at bootstrap: `<USERNAME>/claude_research_config` — the same config repo created during setup. Users with a dedicated tasks repo can override.

## Last updated

<YYYY-MM-DD by bootstrap | by manual edit on YYYY-MM-DD>
